//
// A CONSTANT BUILT WITH TEMPORARIES IS REFUSED, NOT PASTED (`@FR-R-Const`: a constant is a
// value the constant store holds, or code pasted at each use that names no slot of its own).
// `NAMES = ["a", "b"][0..0]` slices a literal, which types as an iterator over the literal's
// temporaries.  Its declaration was refused for needing a temporary, but each use still pasted
// the code, whose slot numbers belong to the declaration and do not index the reading function's
// table: the walk after `main`'s parse panicked with an internal compiler error, and the
// refusal — which names the cure, a zero-argument function — never reached the author
// (loft#2530).  A use of a refused constant now pastes nothing.
//
// @falsified-at: 030f837e6 — the control (the build before it) prints `fatal: internal compiler error` on
//   both backends; here the declaration's refusal, the one error
// CHANNEL: the diagnostic — the control prints an internal compiler error instead.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: has an initialiser that needs a temporary
NAMES = ["a", "b"][0..0];

fn main() {
  n = 0;
  for s in NAMES {
    n += 1;
  }
  println("{n}");
}
